Day 20: Deployment Rolled Back Automatically Within Minutes


Incident:
Production deployment rolled back automatically within 3 minutes.


What Happened Next:
Kubernetes halted rollout after new pods failed readiness checks; rollback is triggered to protect live traffic.


Root Cause:
 1.Readiness Timeout Too Low: Timeout set to 1s, but startup needed 4–5s.
 2.Traffic Sent Too Early: Pods received traffic before stabilizing.


Fix:
 1.Increased readiness timeout to 5s and initialDelay to 10s.
 2.Added minReadySeconds: 30 to enforce stability.


Takeaway:
Readiness probes directly control rollout safety.
